.TH "tangsible-variables" "1" "2026-11-27" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tangsible-variables - where each variable of a host is defined, and which definition wins
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtangsible variables\fR [\fIansible-playbook options\fR .\&.\&.\&] \fIhostname\fR [\fIplaybook.\&yml\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBvariables\fR lists the variables of one inventory host, one line each: the value
of the definition that wins, and the file and line it is written in.\& \fBEnter\fR
(or a click) on a variable shows all its definitions, the winning one first,
in Ansible'\&s own order of precedence, each with its level (for example
\fIinventory group_vars (web)\fR or \fIrole defaults (app)\fR), its value and its place.\&
Nothing is run on any host, and nothing is gathered: only what is written
down is looked at.\&
.PP
The definitions come from the inventory (variables written in the inventory
file, and its \fIgroup_vars\fR and \fIhost_vars\fR), from the \fIgroup_vars\fR and
\fIhost_vars\fR next to the playbook, and from the \fIdefaults\fR and \fIvars\fR of the
roles of the plays that apply to the host.\& If \fIplaybook.\&yml\fR is omitted it is
resolved as for \fBtangsible-run\fR(1) (see \fBtangsible\fR(1)); without a playbook
only the inventory side is listed.\& Several plays applying to the host are
treated as one (their roles together).\&
.PP
When the inventory is in the same directory as the playbook, their shared
\fIgroup_vars\fR and \fIhost_vars\fR are listed once, as the playbook'\&s (the higher
level).\&
.PP
The files are read by Ansible'\&s own code, one source at a time, in the order
of precedence Ansible uses (including a changed \fBVARIABLE_PRECEDENCE\fR).\& Ansible
is also asked for its own answer, and that decides the winner: when it names a
definition other than the one our reading of the order puts first, the
variable is marked with a \fB?\&\fR, Ansible'\&s definition is shown first, and the
order of the other definitions is to be taken with care.\&
.PP
A value written in a vault is shown as \fI<vaulted>\fR.\& A vaulted value that no
given password opens (an unused leftover, say) is shown the same way and does
not stop the list.\&
.PP
Not covered yet: variables of the play itself (\fBvars:\fR, \fBvars_files:\fR) and of
blocks and tasks, gathered facts, and what \fBset_fact\fR and \fBregister\fR create
while a playbook runs.\& \fB-e\fR values given on the command line are listed.\& A
play whose host pattern is templated, and roles included with a computed name,
are not looked at; what was skipped is named under the list.\&
.PP
Standard \fBansible-playbook\fR(1) arguments are passed through (\fB-i\fR,
\fB-e\fR, \fB--vault-password-file\fR, .\&.\&.\&).\& \fB--ask-vault-pass\fR is not supported here:
use a password file.\& Execution environments are not used; the files are read
on the host.\&
.PP
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.PP
\fBUp/Down, Page Up/Down, CTRL-B/F, Home/End, CTRL-A/E\fR
.RS 4
Move the cursor.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEnter\fR
.RS 4
On a variable: show or hide its definitions.\& On a definition: show the
file it is in, with the definition marked and in view.\& The file view is
beside the list on a wide terminal and over it on a narrow one; in it,
\fBUp/Down\fR, \fBPage Up/Down\fR scroll, \fB/\fR and \fBn\fR/\fBN\fR search, \fBy\fR copies the
file, \fBe\fR edits it (and everything is read again afterwards), \fBEsc\fR or \fBq\fR
go back.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBE\fR, \fBC\fR
.RS 4
Show / hide the definitions of every variable.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBRight/Left\fR
.RS 4
The next / previous host of the inventory (the choice of definitions
you opened stays).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBh\fR
.RS 4
Pick a host from a list.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBe\fR
.RS 4
Open the file of the definition under the cursor in \fB$VISUAL\fR / \fB$EDITOR\fR.\&
When the editor returns, everything is read again.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBR\fR
.RS 4
Read the files again.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB?\&\fR, \fBF1\fR
.RS 4
Help.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBq\fR, \fBCTRL-C\fR
.RS 4
Quit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR(1), \fBtangsible-host\fR(1), \fBtangsible-view\fR(1), \fBtangsible-vault\fR(1)
